2026-09-18 01:17:19,338 [INFO] excalibur.core.langfuse: [TOOL]: Bash: {'command': 'python3 << \'PYEOF\'\nimport socket, struct, time\n\n# Let\'s try a completely different approach\n# Maybe the challenge architecture has .10 behind a firewall that only \n# responds to traffic originating from certain networks\n# Or maybe we need to exploit Quagga to create a tunnel\n\n# First, let me check if there are more hosts by examining RIP more carefully\n# RIP response only gave default route (0.0.0.0/0 metric 16 = infinity)\n# Let\'s try to send a RIP request specifically asking for routes\n\n# Build a more complete RIP v2 request\ns = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)\ns.settimeout(3)\n\n# RIP request packet\ncmd = 1  # Request\nver = 2  # Version 2\nrip_pkt = struct.pack(\'!BBH\', cmd, ver, 0)  # command, version, must_be_zero\n# One entry with AFI=0 asks for entire table\nrip_pkt += struct.pack(\'!HHIIII\', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 16)\n\ns.sendto(rip_pkt, (\'10.254.200.1\', 520))\ntry:\n    data, addr = s.recvfrom(8192)\n    print(f"Response from {addr}, length={len(data)}")\n    # Parse\n    cmd, ver, _ = struct.unpack(\'!BBH\', data[:4])\n    print(f"Command={cmd}, Version={ver}")\n    offset = 4\n    entry_num = 0\n    while offset + 20 <= len(data):\n        afi, tag, ip, mask, nexthop, metric = struct.unpack(\'!HHIIII\', data[offset:offset+20])\n        if afi == 0xFFFF:  # Authentication\n            print(f"  Auth entry, skipping")\n            # RIP v2 auth is 20 bytes\n        else:\n            ip_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', ip))\n            mask_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', mask))\n            nh_str = socket.inet_ntoa(struct.pack(\'!I\', nexthop))\n            print(f"  Entry {entry_num}: {ip_str}/{mask_str} nh={nh_str} metric={metric}")\n            entry_num += 1\n        offset += 20\nexcept socket.timeout:\n    print("No response")\ns.close()\nPYEOF', 'description': 'Try connecting to .10 with different source IPs/route